id: pm-github-fmrf
title: Revalidate blocked items against the live state of their GitHub blockers
description: "Add `pm github blockers`: re-read every blocked item (plus non-terminal items whose blocked_by dependency targets an external GitHub reference), parse blocked_reason/description/comments for GitHub references (owner/repo#N, bare #N vs the item repo or --repo, full issue/PR URLs, GH-N), query their current state via batched GraphQL, and report a verdict (cleared / partially_cleared / still_blocked / unresolvable). Report-only: never auto-unblock; --comment appends one idempotent pm comment per cleared item. Exit 0 when nothing cleared, a documented non-zero code when something cleared so CI and the scheduled sync can alert."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-12T10:46:45.720Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T15:25:01.659Z"
assignee: pi-agent
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-gh-blockers
comments[30]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-12T10:46:49.828Z",pi-gh-blockers,"Claimed and started. Companion item: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli-website/blob/main/.agents/pm/features/pm-cli-website-5o9j.toon — this implements the blocker-revalidation capability the companion item calls for, in pm-github where the GitHub client, auth handling and provenance model already live. Design summary: complete pm list read (same receipts as import), candidate selection = status blocked OR non-terminal with an external GitHub blocked_by dependency, reference parsing across blocked_reason/description/comments, batched GraphQL state queries, report-only verdicts, idempotent --comment, wired into the reusable scheduled sync workflow as a report-only step."
  "2026-10-12T10:55:14.500Z",pi-gh-blockers,"Implementation drafted in the package worktree: complete-read refactor (runCompletePmList shared by readPmItems and the new readBlockerPmItems), BlockerPmItem decoder validating blocked_reason/blocked_by/dependencies/comments on top of the existing complete-corpus receipts, reference parser (URL, owner/repo#N, GH-N, name#N, bare #N; gitlab/jira/linear locators masked, github: locator scheme unwrapped), hint resolution against the item's gh: provenance repo then --repo, batched GraphQL state query (issue+pullRequest per number, repos deduped+sorted so recorded fixtures stay stable), verdict function, idempotent --comment with per-item lock, report + exit codes (0 nothing cleared, 4 cleared, 2 usage/token, 1 total state failure). Real GraphQL fixtures recorded from api.github.com: unbraind/pm-cli#854 closed 2026-08-01 (the motivating blocker), #1246 open, PR #34 merged, #999999 not found, plus a repository-not-found and a data-null error response."
  "2026-10-12T11:10:45.144Z",codex-sol,"Continuation audit: prior implementation and fixtures inspected; no gates or workflow integration were completed. Correcting host-rendered reports/exit status, complete SDK reads, GitHub-only dependency selection, partial error handling, and one comment per cleared item before validating. Companion scope remains pm-cli-website-5o9j."
  "2026-10-12T11:18:07.181Z",codex-sol,"Verified prior fixture states live through GitHub GraphQL: pm-cli issue 854 CLOSED/COMPLETED at 2026-08-01T15:24:48Z; PR 34 MERGED at 2026-05-20T21:09:52Z; issue 1246 OPEN. Corrected focused suite passed 23/23 before added CLI/grouped-comment/permission regressions. Complete SDK reader uses listAllComplete with extensions disabled and certifyCompleteListResult. Reports now return structured exit_code for host TOON/JSON rendering. Scheduled reporting step warns on 4 and fails on read errors; comment writes are limited to fully cleared items."
  "2026-10-12T11:24:38.757Z",codex-sol,"Manual acceptance used the built candidate under a distinct isolated extension identity, with explicit --pm-path, no --comment. The current pm-rl corpus is 78 items with zero blocker candidates (exit 0); both motivating items pm-rl-e20d and pm-rl-et5b are now closed. The companion corpus is 937 items with six candidates: two cleared, zero partially_cleared, zero still_blocked, four unresolvable (exit 4). Tracker items, history, and settings remained byte-identical for both runs. The complete SDK read refreshed only ignored pm-rl runtime metadata caches. No companion content or private blocker prose was copied into package evidence."
  "2026-10-12T11:27:23.884Z",codex-sol,"Additional corrections: reports expose only requested item identities/status and parsed reference state, omitting full blocker prose/title from workflow logs. Annotations group newly cleared references in one comment per fully cleared item; partial query/permission or annotation failures return report + exit 1. Lock degradation now fails closed rather than permitting duplicate-prone unlocked comments. Peer/manifest floor raised together to PM CLI 2026.10.5 for required SDK and host exit_code contracts; README discloses the compatibility change."
  "2026-10-12T11:34:26.749Z",codex-sol,"Behavioural revert proof in isolated source copies: replacing only parseBlockerReferences with its absent-parser behavior (empty references) made both the all-forms regression and real-tracker mixed scenario fail: 0/2 pass, exit 1. Replacing only blockerItemVerdict with the old static blocked behavior (still_blocked) made both verdict regression and real-tracker mixed scenario fail: 0/2 pass, exit 1. Production source remained intact. Scheduled report executable acceptance passed 1/1: code 4 becomes a warning and preserves item bytes; query failure remains exit 1. The first diagnostic full suite exposed installed global extension SDK/host skew in scratch health checks; workflow fixtures now isolate their global extension root."
  "2026-10-12T11:38:57.331Z",codex-sol,"Corrected companion permalink after checking its canonical remote: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli-companion/blob/main/.agents/pm/features/pm-cli-website-5o9j.toon . The original pi comment used the legacy pm-cli-website repository name; the owner item id remains pm-cli-website-5o9j."
  "2026-10-12T11:39:35.124Z",codex-sol,"Final linked regression run: pm test pm-github-fmrf --run --progress --timeout 600 passed the linked npm run build && node --test test/blockers.test.ts command, 30/30 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos. The earlier default 120-second linked run timed out on the shared host; the expanded run completed in about 136 seconds. Test-result tracking is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment records the completed evidence without altering tracker settings."
  "2026-10-12T11:55:13.486Z",codex-sol,"Frozen-source npm release certification passed with CI identity isolation: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check. Result: 551/551 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos; exact 100/100/100/100 coverage across all 12 authored modules at unchanged thresholds. Typecheck, build, 150 documented declarations, lint, zero duplication, privacy, production audit, pack dry-run, changelog check, and publish-attestation checks passed. Source checksums stayed unchanged throughout the run."
  "2026-10-12T12:06:27.255Z",codex-sol,"Packed live consumer acceptance passed 2/2 scenarios with the same npm archive installed into a scratch tracker: Node first read two distinct closed/merged references deduplicated from all requested forms, returned exit 4 and appended one grouped comment. An actual native Bun CLI run returned exit 4, skipped the existing comment, and appended zero duplicates. The scratch item retained status blocked. All GitHub calls were observational; no --comment was used on fleet or companion trackers."
  "2026-10-12T12:07:13.194Z",codex-sol,"Bun release certification passed on unchanged source with CI identity isolation: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 bun run release:check. Result: 551/551 tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos; all 12 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage with unchanged thresholds. All release checks passed, including privacy, zero duplication, audit, packing, changelog, and attestation. Both Node/npm and Bun runner gates execute the package coverage suite under Node; native Bun behavior was separately accepted through the installed packed CLI. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; no release, tag, publication, merge, or fleet/companion item mutation was performed."
  "2026-10-12T12:14:48.658Z",codex-sol,"Review PR opened: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/115 on feat/blocker-revalidation. Implementation and regression sources match the frozen source certified by both release gates; all tracked work and receipts are committed as SteveBot. CI and reviews are pending on the final PR head and are not claimed as approval. Item remains in_progress, unclaimed, for orchestrator verification. CLI UX encountered: installed project extensions shadowed the candidate and emitted a generic unknown-option error; isolated candidate identity was used for live acceptance. Unrelated installed global extension SDK/host skew contaminated scratch health until the fixtures isolated their global extension root. No CLI/SDK issue was filed."
  "2026-10-12T12:23:45.555Z",codex-sol,"Final-head CodeQL reported a genuine polynomial regular expression risk in blocker comment marker extraction (alert 5): the broad repository capture could consume repeated marker openers before failing on a missing number. Reclaimed the item to fix this before handoff. Replacing that capture with the same GitHub owner/repo grammar used by reference resolution, and preventing timestamp captures from crossing HTML delimiters; adding a bounded subprocess regression against the reported repeated-prefix payload. Earlier gate receipts remain valid for their frozen source, but both gates will be rerun for the correction."
  "2026-10-12T12:44:03.202Z",codex-sol,"Marker remediation verified: focused marker/idempotency cases passed 4/4; restoring only the old regex made the bounded repeated-prefix regression fail at its 10-second deadline (0/1 pass, exit 1). The corrected parser/marker protocol also preserves valid .github-style repo names and HTTP/case variants. Provenance hints now pass the same repository grammar before entering GraphQL; unresolved GH-N/#N mentions deduplicate consistently. Focused related regressions passed 11/11. Freezing this correction and rerunning both complete release gates with independent coverage directories."
  "2026-10-12T12:51:37.633Z",codex-sol,"Corrected-source live acceptance repeated: pm-rl 78 items/zero candidates/exit 0; companion 937 items/six candidates/two cleared/four unresolvable/exit 4. Item/history/settings bytes remained unchanged. The newly packed corrected artifact also passed Node and native Bun acceptance 2/2: two resolved references, one grouped scratch comment on Node, zero duplicate comments on Bun, status still blocked. No --comment was used outside scratch trackers."
  "2026-10-12T12:58:08.241Z",codex-sol,"Corrected pm-linked blocker suite passed 32/32, zero failures/skips/cancellations/todos, using pm test pm-github-fmrf --run --only-index 1 --progress --timeout 600. The marker performance test and repository/provenance regressions are included. Both complete release runs have passed their adversarial workflow fixtures; final receipts remain pending."
  "2026-10-12T13:03:23.942Z",codex-sol,"Corrected-source final certification supersedes the earlier source receipts: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed with required HOME/Git identity isolation, 553/553 tests each and zero failure/skip/cancel/todo. Bun ran in an identical isolated source copy with independent coverage output. Both coverage receipts matched: 12 authored modules, 9486/9486 lines and statements, 232/232 functions, 2484/2484 branches, exact 100/100/100/100 at unchanged thresholds. All remaining release checks passed. Linked suite 32/32, scheduled acceptance 1/1, packed Node/native Bun 2/2, parser/verdict revert proofs 0/2 each, old-marker-regex revert 0/1 with bounded timeout. Implementation/test checksums stayed unchanged across these runs. Pushing the correction to PR 115 for final-head CodeQL verification."
  "2026-10-12T13:12:30.216Z",codex-sol,"Final correction 50c41c6166d9333e2259e8dc9b3ead68a3ade4da reached PR 115 after transient commit_refs push rejections. CodeQL results check 114825479059 succeeded with No new alerts and zero annotations; the codeql workflow and Semgrep also succeeded. The previous polynomial marker alert is remediated. Node 22/26 CI is still running; neutral/skipped/unavailable reviewers are not approval. All implementation/test bytes remain identical to the npm/Bun 553-test, exact-coverage receipts. Claim remains released and item in_progress for orchestrator verification. No merges, tags, releases or publications were made."
  "2026-10-13T12:06:42.543Z",codex-agent,"Revalidating PR #115 against current main. Confirmed the host TOON scalar assertion failure and own-provenance blocker contamination. Will parse rendered output, exclude all own provenance keys, add unit and real-tracker regressions, prove failure with only collectBlockerReferences reverted, and rerun unchanged npm/Bun release gates. CI also showed a telemetry cleanup race; investigating during validation."
  "2026-10-13T12:12:13.255Z",codex-agent,"Both review findings are fixed. TOON CLI output is decoded through the installed host parser and asserted structurally. collectBlockerReferences excludes every own provenance key after resolution. New unit and real-tracker regressions pass 2/2, covering mixed-case tags, multiple provenance keys, all text sources, cross-repository blockers, true cleared annotations and false-clearance prevention without status changes. CI telemetry teardown now uses bounded recursive-remove retries; no telemetry configuration changed. Behavioral revert and full PM-linked/npm/Bun validation are running."
  "2026-10-13T12:14:12.776Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof passed: in a disposable candidate copy, restoring only collectBlockerReferences while keeping both new tests unchanged made both fail by assertion (0/2 pass, exit 1). The unit restored two own-provenance keys; the real-tracker scenario failed its clearance/exit assertion when the unwanted own issue contaminated the query. Command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"imported blocker candidates|collectBlockerReferences excludes\" test/blockers.test.ts. Fixed source passed the same command 2/2; production source stayed unchanged and these tests import TypeScript, so no dist rebuild was required. The initial disposable-copy attempt lacked a sibling module and was discarded as infrastructure failure, not revert evidence."
  "2026-10-13T12:23:21.752Z",codex-agent,"PM-linked blocker suite hit its 600-second run budget under shared-runner contention; this is a timeout receipt, not acceptance. The scheduled-report linked command is still running. Increasing the blocker suite stored budget to 1200 seconds and queuing its rerun after full release gates finish to reduce duplicated load. Full coverage currently reports no assertion failures; exact npm/Bun gate receipts remain pending."
  "2026-10-13T13:35:26.787Z",codex-agent,"The sibling PR release run exposed an outer native Bun fixture timeout during packing/setup plus the initial Node import. Increased only the outer fixture budget from 180 to 900 seconds in both branches; the three native Bun repeats still each enforce the unchanged 45-second runtime deadline and byte/exit assertions. Stopped the superseded npm run before restarting against this test change; its partial receipt is not a passing gate. Queuing clean npm/Bun gates and isolated PM-linked execution. The blocker collection code and its 2/2 positive, 0/2 assertion-based behavioral revert proof remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-13T14:06:22.744Z",pi-agent,"Continuation takeover (previous agent stopped for quota). Re-reviewing the 5 uncommitted files in the package worktree, then merging current main (which now includes PR #116) and re-validating both CodeRabbit findings: the own-provenance blocker reference fix and the TOON quoting test. The local packed-Bun fixture timeout stays a runner-contention artifact, so its 180-second outer budget will be restored rather than raised."
  "2026-10-13T14:08:23.881Z",pi-agent,"Merged current main (includes PR #116) cleanly into this branch; both features coexist (import-issue selection symbols and the own-provenance exclusion are all present) and tsc build passes. Re-verified the behavioural revert proof on the merged tree: reverting only collectBlockerReferences (keeping both new regressions unchanged) made both fail by assertion (0/2 pass, exit 1); restoring the function made the same command pass 2/2. Command: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"collectBlockerReferences excludes|imported blocker candidates\" test/blockers.test.ts with isolated HOME/Git identity. The local packed-Bun fixture timeout was restored to its unchanged 180-second outer budget (runner contention is not a bug); the bounded-retry teardown fix for the CI ENOTEMPTY telemetry race is kept. Full npm/Bun release gates and the PM-linked suite are running next."
  "2026-10-13T14:53:04.319Z",pi-agent,"Final merged-tree certification: PM-linked suite passed (blockers 34/34 including both new regressions, scheduled blocker report 1/1). npm run release:check passed with CI identity isolation: 581/581 tests, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo, 12 authored modules at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage with unchanged thresholds and inventories; the packed native-Bun fixture passed at its unchanged 180-second outer budget, confirming the earlier timeout was runner contention. bun run release:check passed identically: 581/581 tests, exact 100/100/100/100 coverage, zero failures. All release-chain checks passed in both runs: typecheck, build, docstrings, lint, zero duplication, privacy, audit, packing, changelog, publish attestation. Pushing the merged head for CI verification."
  "2026-10-13T14:57:32.923Z",pi-agent,"CI on the pushed merged head failed the tracked-project health gate on pm-github-fmrf history drift (chain and hash mismatch): the previous session's last eight records stored hashes that do not match recomputation. Reproduced locally, confirmed all patches replay with zero content loss, and ran the sanctioned history repair (recompute chain, audited history_repair marker). Health is now fully green under CI-identical isolation; the local extension-host version-skew warning came from unrelated globally installed extension copies on this host, absent in CI. Repair committed and pushed; watching CI on the new head."
  "2026-10-13T15:17:06.146Z",pi-agent,"CI is green on the final pushed head after the history re-anchor: test (22) pass, test (26) pass, codeql/CodeQL pass, semgrep pass, CodeRabbit completed without new findings. The PR is mergeable against current main; only required approvals block the merge, which is left to the orchestrator. Both review findings remain fixed at this head: own-provenance blocker exclusion with its unit and real-tracker regressions, and structural TOON output assertions through the installed host parser. No merge, tag, release or publication was performed."
  "2026-10-13T15:25:01.659Z",pi-agent,"Root cause found for the recurring history drift: pm writes made with the globally installed pm-cli (2026.10.13) compute item hashes differently from this repository's pinned pm-cli (2026.10.9), which CI's health gate uses to re-verify. The previous session's writes and my own final comment used the global binary, breaking the chain hash at each boundary despite identical replayed patches and no content loss. All further writes in this tracker go through the repository's pinned pm binary, and the chain is being re-anchored again by it."
